* =============================================================================
* BF961  N-channel dual-gate depletion MOSFET  (Vishay / Telefunken)
* =============================================================================
*
* WHAT THIS FILE IS
*   An ngspice subcircuit that behaves like a BF961 for this mixer project.
*   It is a behavioural model DERIVED FROM THE DATASHEET, not a vendor model:
*   no manufacturer SPICE model for the BF961 could be found. It is good for
*   DC bias, switching by gate 2 and the low-frequency (kHz) IF behaviour.
*   It is NOT meant for accurate noise, VHF gain or S-parameter work.
*
* HOW A DUAL-GATE MOSFET IS MODELLED
*   A dual-gate MOSFET is physically one channel with two gates in series
*   along it. Electrically it acts like two ordinary MOSFETs stacked on top of
*   each other (a "cascode"):
*
*            D (drain)
*            |
*       G2 --| M2   upper device, controlled by gate 2
*            |
*            X      internal node between the two gates (not a real pin)
*            |
*       G1 --| M1   lower device, controlled by gate 1
*            |
*            S (source, also the substrate/bulk)
*
*   Gate 1 normally carries the signal (here: the RF), gate 2 sets the gain
*   (AGC in a normal amplifier; here: the LO, which switches the gain on and
*   off, and that is what makes the circuit a mixer).
*   Both devices are DEPLETION mode: they conduct with 0 V gate-source voltage
*   and need a NEGATIVE gate voltage to turn off (VTO < 0).
*
* DATASHEET VALUES USED FOR THE FIT  (Tamb = 25 C)
*   IDSS   = 4 ... 20 mA            @ VDS=15 V, VG1S=0, VG2S=4 V
*            -> model gives 9.7 mA (middle of the range)
*   |y21s| = 15 mS typ, 12 mS min   @ VDS=15 V, ID=10 mA, VG2S=4 V, f=1 MHz
*            -> model gives 15.1 mS  (y21s = forward transadmittance = gm)
*   -VG1S(off) <= 3.5 V             @ VDS=15 V, VG2S=4 V, ID=20 uA
*            -> model gives 1.24 V
*   -VG2S(off) <= 3.5 V             @ VDS=15 V, VG1S=0, ID=20 uA
*            -> model gives 0.96 V
*   (the datasheet only gives a maximum for the cut-off voltages; the chosen
*    values agree with the shape of datasheet Figs. 2 to 4, where the drain
*    current is already near zero at VG1S = -1.2 V)
*   Cissg1 = 3.7 pF, Cissg2 = 1.6 pF, Crss = 25 fF, Coss = 1.6 pF
*   Integrated gate protection diodes, V(BR)G1SS = V(BR)G2SS = 8 ... 14 V
*   Absolute max: VDS 20 V, ID 30 mA, Ptot 200 mW
*
* HOW THE FIT WAS DONE
*   Level-1 (square-law) MOSFET: in saturation ID = (KP/2)(W/L)(VGS-VTO)^2,
*   so gm = 2*ID/(VGS-VTO).
*   - M1 sets IDSS and gm. With gm = 15 mS at ID = 10 mA, VGS-VTO = 1.33 V,
*     so VTO1 = -1.3 V; KP1 then follows from IDSS ~ 10 mA at VG1S = 0.
*   - M2 must be "stronger" than M1 (larger KP) so that with VG2S = 4 V it
*     never limits the current, and its VTO2 = -1.0 V sets the gate-2 cut-off.
*   - The values were then checked with a DC sweep (run.py "model check"),
*     which prints the table in plots/results.txt and plots/bf961_model.png.
*
* KNOWN LIMITS
*   - Square law: gm keeps growing with VG1S instead of flattening out as in
*     datasheet Fig. 4.
*   - Capacitances are fixed values; in the real part they vary with bias.
*   - No noise sources, no temperature dependence.
*   - Real parts spread over IDSS = 4 ... 20 mA; this models one typical part.
*
* PIN ORDER (use this order in the X line of the netlist)
*   D   drain
*   G2  gate 2
*   G1  gate 1
*   S   source (the substrate/bulk is tied to the source inside the part)
* =============================================================================
.subckt BF961 D G2 G1 S

* ----- the two stacked transistors -------------------------------------------
* Syntax: Mname drain gate source bulk model L=length W=width
* M1 = lower device: drain on the internal node X, gate = G1, source = S.
M1 X  G1 S S NG1 L=1u W=100u
* M2 = upper device: drain = D, gate = G2, source on the internal node X.
*      Its bulk is tied to S (as in the real part, the whole channel sits in
*      one substrate); GAMMA=0 below means the body effect is ignored anyway.
M2 D  G2 X S NG2 L=1u W=100u

* ----- terminal capacitances from the datasheet ------------------------------
* A level-1 model without TOX has no internal capacitances, so the datasheet
* values are added as plain capacitors between the pins.
Cg1 G1 S 3.7p      ; Cissg1: gate 1 input capacitance
Cg2 G2 S 1.6p      ; Cissg2: gate 2 input capacitance
Crs G1 D 25f       ; Crss: feedback capacitance gate 1 -> drain
Cos D  S 1.6p      ; Coss: output capacitance

* ----- gate protection diodes ------------------------------------------------
* The BF961 has two zener diodes back to back between each gate and the
* source. Below about +/-10 V they do nothing (only tiny leakage); above that
* they conduct and protect the thin gate oxide. Modelled as two diodes in
* series, cathode to cathode, through a private middle node (P1, P2):
*   G1 -->|-- P1 --|<-- S   (DG1a anode on G1, DG1b anode on S)
* Syntax: Dname anode cathode model   (here P1/P2 are the common cathodes)
* Whichever polarity the gate goes, one diode is forward biased and the other
* one breaks down at BV, so the gate is clamped at about +/-(BV + 0.7 V).
DG1a G1 P1 DZ
DG1b S  P1 DZ
DG2a G2 P2 DZ
DG2b S  P2 DZ

* ----- drain-substrate junction ----------------------------------------------
* The parasitic diode between substrate (= source, anode) and drain
* (cathode). Normally reverse biased because the drain is positive; it would
* only conduct if the drain went below the source. BV=25 V puts its breakdown
* above the 20 V VDS rating.
DDS S D DSUB

* ----- model cards -----------------------------------------------------------
* NG1: lower device (gate 1).
*   LEVEL=1   Shichman-Hodges square-law model (simple, robust)
*   VTO=-1.3  threshold voltage in V; negative = depletion mode
*   KP=110u   transconductance parameter in A/V^2 (with W/L=100 -> 11 mA/V^2)
*   LAMBDA    channel-length modulation, gives a little output conductance
*             (the slight upward slope of the ID-VDS curves)
*   GAMMA=0   no body effect; PHI is then unused but kept for completeness
.model NG1 NMOS (LEVEL=1 VTO=-1.3 KP=110u LAMBDA=0.01 GAMMA=0 PHI=0.6)
* NG2: upper device (gate 2). Larger KP (20 mA/V^2) so that it does not limit
* the current when gate 2 is high; VTO=-1.0 V sets the gate-2 cut-off.
.model NG2 NMOS (LEVEL=1 VTO=-1.0 KP=200u LAMBDA=0.02 GAMMA=0 PHI=0.6)
* DZ: protection zener. BV=10 V reverse breakdown (datasheet 8 ... 14 V),
* IBV = current at which BV is defined, RS = series resistance.
.model DZ D (IS=1e-14 BV=10 IBV=1m RS=5)
* DSUB: drain-substrate junction, 0.5 pF junction capacitance at 0 V.
.model DSUB D (IS=1e-14 BV=25 CJO=0.5p)

.ends BF961
